Write this client's first 7 day diet. Build it from the food they already eat. The daily tracker reads every day, so each day is written in full.

CLIENT DETAILS:
[CLIENT DETAILS]

HOW TO WRITE IT:

1. Start with the meals. A one or two sentence opener is enough. Do not mention a coaching week number. NEVER write "Welcome to week" or a cross-day pointer.

2. The only daily calorie target is the CALORIE METHOD number, within 100 kcal. Do not replace it with a floor and do not invent a different deficit. Fat loss is 350 kcal below maintenance on steady, 300 on build-up, and 250 on high flux. Muscle gain is 150 kcal above on steady, 200 on build-up, and 250 on high flux. Recomp is maintenance. Those cuts are already inside CALORIE METHOD. Write that number.
   If the allowed foods cannot hit a high protein number, lower the protein and keep the calories. Do not cut rice, roti, oil, or snacks to chase grams. Never print a protein or calorie number higher than the food on the plate.

3. Use their meal times and their usual breakfast, lunch, dinner, and snack. Adjust portions. At most one swap per meal. Do not replace their plate with a new menu. If they eat lunch at 2pm, lunch stays near 2pm. Do not put a dinner time on breakfast.

4. For each meal write one primary option in a plain sentence, with household portions and grams. Example: "2 rotis with 1 katori cooked dal, about 150g, and a bowl of sabzi." After that option, the next line is the macro line for that option only: (P: 28g | C: 45g | F: 12g | ~400 kcal). A swap, if you offer one, gets its own macro line. Daily Total and the header count the primary option only. Never add the primary and the swap together. Name the cooking fat in teaspoons. Oil only for a vegan. End each day with Daily Total.

5. Diet preference is non negotiable. Vegetarian: no egg, chicken, fish, or meat on any day. Vegan: no milk, curd, paneer, ghee, butter, cheese, whey, honey, egg, or meat. Eggetarian: eggs only on the weekdays in Hard Constraints, and never chicken or fish. Non vegetarian: egg, chicken, or fish only on the weekdays listed for that food. If no egg days are listed, write zero eggs. If no chicken days are listed, write zero chicken. If no fish days are listed, write zero fish. Every other day is fully vegetarian. Do not add eggs just because the person eats chicken. On an allowed day, include that food unless they dislike it. Never use an allergy or a disliked food. If they do not use whey, do not write whey.

6. Obey their variety choice. Same daily means the same plates, still written out in full under every day. Different daily means most days change the plate. The daily tracker cannot resolve cross-day references. NEVER write "same as Monday", "repeat Tuesday", or "as above". Copy the full meal text under each day.

7. Cover Day 1 (Monday) through Day 7 (Sunday). After Day 7, one short closing line and one short note on how long the goal may take with their real schedule. No tips section. Never use a hyphen, en dash, or em dash. Write "10 to 15" not "10-15".

8. If anything here conflicts with Hard Constraints, obey Hard Constraints.
